      "statement": "ExecutionSession exposes `events: AsyncIterable<ExecutionEventCreateInput>` (persisted + broadcast by processEventStream), `result: Promise<ExecutionResult>`, `closed?: Promise<void>` (resolves only after the OS child and its streams close), mandatory `cancel()`, and optional, currently-unimplemented `pause()`/`resume()`.",
