    {
      "id": "claim_93047d37bd174a2d9e9e50310b557285",
      "statement": "ExecutionFailure carries `retryable` and `sideEffectsPossible`; the engine's normalizeFailure forces retryable=false whenever sideEffectsPossible is true, and nextRetryExecutor refuses any retry if attempt >= maxRetries, !failure.retryable, or failure.sideEffectsPossible — so post-side-effect failures never chain-hop providers.",
